<wpt lat="24.079999" lon="32.919998">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Aswan</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA169&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Aswan%22&quot;&gt;Strana 169&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;Below Alexandria lay the town of Syene, the modern &lt;b&gt;Aswan&lt;/b&gt;. At noon on the longest day of the year the sun&amp;#39;s rays illuminated a deep well at Syene, &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA169&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Aswan%22&quot;&gt;Strana 169&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="33.330001" lon="44.439998">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Baghdad</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA233&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Baghdad%22&quot;&gt;Strana 233&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;He crossed Arabia to the mouth of the Euphrates, paralleled the Tigris upstream past &lt;b&gt;Baghdad&lt;/b&gt; into Turkey, and returned to Mecca where he spent the &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA233&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Baghdad%22&quot;&gt;Strana 233&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="34.819999" lon="67.519996">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Bamiyan</name>
