<wpt lat="41.85" lon="-87.65">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Chicago</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA185&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Chicago%22&quot;&gt;Strana 185&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;Although I once knew a man in &lt;b&gt;Chicago&lt;/b&gt; who had an impressive collection of walrus and whale penises, which proves that just about anything will appeal &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA185&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Chicago%22&quot;&gt;Strana 185&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="50.940664" lon="6.959911">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Cologne</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA271&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Cologne%22&quot;&gt;Strana 271&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;Traveling through the countryside they might forage enough to keep themselves alive, but they could not camp day after day in the streets of &lt;b&gt;Cologne&lt;/b&gt;. &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA271&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Cologne%22&quot;&gt;Strana 271&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="55.68" lon="12.569999">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Copenhagen</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA44&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Copenhagen%22&quot;&gt;Strana 44&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;Now in &lt;b&gt;Copenhagen&lt;/b&gt;, in the basement of that peculiar Edwardian museum known as the Glyptothek, are several bona fide Etruscan figures: a shattered &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA44&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Copenhagen%22&quot;&gt;Strana 44&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="24.799999" lon="-107.389999">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Culiacan</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA390&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Culiacan%22&quot;&gt;Strana 390&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;That autumn Coronado led what remained of his army across the deserts and mountains into Sinaloa where, at &lt;b&gt;Culiacan&lt;/b&gt;, it was disbanded. &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA390&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Culiacan%22&quot;&gt;Strana 390&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="33.5" lon="36.319999">
  <ele>0</ele>
  <name>Damascus</name>
  <desc>&lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA276&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Damascus%22&quot;&gt;Strana 276&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;Consequently we have no idea if he drowned in the surf at Accipitrum, or was beheaded at &lt;b&gt;Damascus&lt;/b&gt;, or spent his life in the fields near Alexandria, &lt;b&gt;...&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;more pages:  &lt;a href=&quot;http://books.google.com/books?id=BKpZAAAAMAAJ&amp;amp;pg=PA276&amp;amp;hl=cs&amp;amp;vq=%22Damascus%22&quot;&gt;Strana 276&lt;/a&gt;</desc>
</wpt>
